[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2552576514","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100543#issuecomment-2552576514","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100543","id":2552576514,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YJToC","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T01:18:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-19T01:18:55Z","body":"Can't reproduce issue in MRP. Well, in any case that should be the intended behavior. If you are using AnimationTree you should review the settings for Discrete since String will be interpolated to animate the characters if it is Continuous. Make sure that the UpdateMode of the animation track is set to Discrete, and then set CallbackModeDiscrete to something other than ForceContinuous.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98fd62ec-0f1a-4748-b0fa-f6148edcfae6)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48132d76-2e46-4224-8176-592504f835ca)\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://